domain ADR0032Review:
  description "Formal review of exact ADR0032 revision 1. Candidate status remains Proposed."
problem P1:
  |
    Determine whether the candidate coherently corrects unsupported elapsed-time
    semantics without weakening accepted accounting, fencing, retry authority or
    ADR lifecycle requirements.
evidence E1:
  |
    The reviewed authoritative candidate SHA256 is
    c9e8ee12edd8f57d796ab389958c8a8f741011fd853b49662f265291bbdb8409.
evidence E2:
  |
    ADR0032 D1 separates provider transport timeout, worker execution boundary,
    semantic progress termination and cumulative non-time resource ceilings.
evidence E3:
  |
    ADR0032 D2 rejects whole-attempt wall clock as semantic failure, prohibits silent
    consumption restart, and D5 explicitly retains all ADR0031 boundaries other than
    the stated D7 elapsed-time refinement.
evidence E4:
  |
    Accepted ADR0031 D6 requires process or lease loss to terminalize the claimed run
    through fenced recovery with conservative in-flight accounting; an explicit owner
    retry creates a new attempt. ADR0031 D9 distinguishes technical from semantic
    failure.
evidence E5:
  |
    ADR0032 D3 permits continuation after provider timeout only when an explicitly
    accepted bounded recovery remains, and D4 with U1 keeps the recovery policy, cost
    and exact values pending a later evidence-backed owner decision.
evidence E6:
  |
    ADR0032 D4 denies activation authority until exact route, platform, evidence and
    policy are accepted. D5 separately denies implementation, provider calls,
    deployment, route selection and production activation.
evidence E7:
  |
    Repository ADR rules require an accepted ADR that changes ADR0031 to mark ADR0031
    Superseded with a link. ADR0032 is still Proposed, and ADR0031 D10 expressly says
    no old ADR is marked Superseded while the successor is Proposed.
evidence E8:
  |
    Command-line audit of ADR0032 reports zero fatal, error and warning findings; its
    one information item is the deliberately pending owner acceptance.
premise C1:
  |
    D5's retention clause resolves D2 under ADR0031 D6 and D9: a worker-boundary event
    may preserve a recoverable technical receipt but cannot resume the same claimed run
    or reset consumption. Owner retry remains a new attempt.
premise C2:
  |
    D3 is a guarded extension point, not retry authority. With no separately accepted
    bounded recovery, the condition is false and the candidate authorizes no automatic
    retry or extra paid call.
premise C3:
  |
    Deferring exact time values is coherent because the candidate fixes the boundary
    meanings, records the missing evidence, and expressly blocks activation until the
    numerical policy is separately accepted.
premise C4:
  |
    The required ADR0031 Superseded status and reciprocal link are acceptance-time
    lifecycle effects. They must accompany a later acceptance record, but need not
    mutate either ADR while ADR0032 remains Proposed.
pending L1:
  |
    This review was performed in the current task by the same agent because no
    independent or delegated reviewer was requested. It is a formal content review,
    not identity-independent corroboration.
decision D1 based_on P1, E1, E2, E3, E4, C1:
  |
    Record no P0 through P3 finding for worker-boundary semantics. Same-attempt resume
    would contradict the retained contract, so it is not authorized by this candidate.
decision D2 based_on P1, E1, E5, E6, C2, C3:
  |
    Record no P0 through P3 finding for provider timeout or missing numeric values.
    The exact recovery and numerical policy remain later owner decisions and cannot be
    inferred during implementation.
decision D3 based_on P1, E1, E7, C4:
  |
    Record no candidate finding for lifecycle status while Proposed. If the owner later
    accepts this exact revision, the acceptance transaction must mark ADR0031
    Superseded, link it to ADR0032, and preserve its retained decisions through D5.
decision D4 based_on P1, E1, E8, D1, D2, D3, L1:
  |
    Complete REVIEW with PASS, zero P0-P3 findings, and recommend owner ACCEPT for the
    exact revision. Do not accept or edit the candidate and do not authorize code,
    provider, deployment, activation, commit or push effects.
